mn2:6.3 starts: the unarisen effluent of becoming arises in him
mn2:6.4 starts: the unarisen effluent of ignorance arises in him
mn2:6.8 starts: the unarisen effluent of becoming doesn’t arise in him
mn2:10.3 starts: the unarisen effluent of becoming arises in him
mn2:10.4 starts: the unarisen effluent of ignorance arises in him
mn2:10.8 starts: the unarisen effluent of becoming doesn’t arise in him
mn2:15.2 starts: simply to counteract cold, to counteract heat,
mn2:16.2 starts: simply to counteract any pains of illness
mn82:8.16 starts: You know nothing of suffering.
mn82:8.18 starts: Get up, dear. Eat, drink, & enjoy yourself.
mn82:8.19 starts: While eating, drinking, & looking after yourself,
mn82:8.20 starts: We don’t give our permission for you
mn82:8.21 starts: Even with your death we would not
mn82:8.22 starts: so how could we—while you’re alive—give
